// The nightly CLI tools update, its check-and-ingest half (#550). Tom, 2026-10-14 (AGENTS.md):
// "nightly, i want to be chekcing codex and cc and other programs for their latest version and
// ingesting it, potentially also with the new features that they entail".
// update-check does every mechanical step: one rolling update/<input> PR per watched input of
// lib/update-watch.json. This brief adds the builder guard and the digest (update-check skill §2).
// It merges and switches nothing; the flash half is fleet-nightly.
// It runs in the master agency on the NAS, where gh, git and the credentials live. The gate's
// builds go to the Nix builder, strix-coordinator; the NAS builds nothing itself.
// Step 3 is the digest, which the update-check skill writes only when Tom asks: arming this item
// is that ask. Delete step 3 to keep the check alone.
{
  "name": "CLI tools update check",
  // Off (Tom, 11 Nov: "make sure there are no scheduled work in the morning").
  // Tom arms it: scheduled set master:cli-update enabled true
  "enabled": false,
  "on": {
    "schedule": [
      // After fleet-nightly's 01:00, outside the 02:00-02:59 DST gap.
      { "cron": "30 1 * * *", "timezone": "Europe/Paris" },
      // One more chance when 01:30 deferred for load or a busy agent. update-check's
      // night stamp answers already-checked when 01:30 completed.
      { "cron": "30 4 * * *", "timezone": "Europe/Paris" }
    ]
  },
  "job": {
    "prompt": [
      "You are in the master agency on the NAS. Run every command here; update-check needs this host's gh and git credentials.",
      "The night key is the date of the Due or Requested time in the header minus 12 hours.",
      "0. Preconditions, read-only. Run: ssh -o BatchMode=yes strix-coordinator df -BG --output=avail / and quote the number. If it shows less than 25G, say so and end: update-check's gate builds on that builder.",
      "Run: nix config show max-jobs, then nix config show builders; when that starts with @, read the file it names. If max-jobs is not 0, or no builder line names strix-coordinator, quote both and end. Never name or use strix-worker as a target.",
      "1. Run exactly: update-check --if-idle --background --json. Quote the JSON. When update-check is not on PATH, it is ~/.local/bin/update-check.",
      "deferred: quote the reasons and end. already-checked: quote the previous night's result and end; a previous failure stays a failure to report. Do not retry it, remove the night stamp or run without --if-idle.",
      "2. If launched: read the job file the receipt names every 5 minutes until its status is completed, error or interrupted, for at most 3 h 30. Then write one line per input: status, PR or issue link, versions, gate error.",
      "On error or interrupted, quote the error and the last 20 lines of the job log, and do not relaunch.",
      "3. For each input whose status is opened or refreshed, follow the update-check skill section 2 once: read the PR body and every release it spans, then write or edit the one <!-- update-digest <to_rev> --> comment on that PR (Worth taking, Touches us, Nothing for us). Plain words, upstream text only inside literal fences, no @mentions or #refs as active Markdown. This is the only write besides what update-check does itself.",
      "Never: merge, approve, close or label a PR; push to main; run nixos-rebuild, switch-to-configuration, a deploy or nix flake update in ~/mecattaf/dotfiles; start, stop or restart a unit; edit lib/update-watch.json or flake.nix; start fleet-update; touch ~/.local/state/update-check except through update-check.",
      "End with one line: deferred (reasons), already-checked, completed (n PRs, n digests), or the error, quoted."
    ]
  }
}
